@prefix chorus: <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# #3870 — Service ONE of nine: Identity. Pair-review copy (kade drafts, wren
# navigates, silas gates — authN is his domain per Jeff's 2026-07-24 cut).
# BOUNDARY (issuance-only — wren's red-line 16:04 applied): a running thing
# is INSIDE Identity iff it MINTS who-you-are — issues tokens, holds signing
# keys, publishes JWKS, owns WebIDs. VERIFICATION IS A LIBRARY consumers
# embed: the verify code runs inside chorus-api, the app, the clearing — those
# instances deploy to THEIR Services, not to Identity. Two people agree at
# instance level: does this process mint identity? CSS pod: yes, inside — and
# it is Identity's ONLY instance (com.security.css). chorus-api verifying a
# token: outside. authorized-users.ts deciding access: outside (authZ).

chorus:service-identity a chorus:Service ;
    rdfs:label "Identity" ; chorus:label "Identity" ;
    chorus:overview "Who anyone is, human or agent — the one place identity is MINTED for the whole system. The CSS Solid pod on :3001 is the OIDC issuer (public door id.lightlifeurbangardens.com via the tunnel); the #3613 seam issues agents client-credential identities (ES256, JWKS published for consumers to verify with); the shared-session cookie key (~/.chorus/share-oidc.json) lets surfaces verify a browser session without re-asking. Everything downstream that decides permissions consumes this service's answers; nothing else may mint them." ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:role-silas ;
    chorus:status "operating" ;
    chorus:asIs "Live: CSS pod issues for jeff + all three role Principals (webIds reconciled #3726, reproducible from MODEL_SET); seam verification is deployed on chorus-api's envelope door; login on the gathering app performs the client-credentials grant server-side, spoofing the public issuer Host because Cloudflare 1010-blocks the direct call. Hard truths from the live walk: login FAILS HARD when :3001 is down (no fallback page, error render), and Identity is a single instance on one machine." ;
    chorus:toBe "Every participant on every public surface authenticates through this seam — the Clearing door included (#3669 lanes 2-3): agents via client-credentials with DPoP, humans via browser OIDC against id.lightlifeurbangardens.com, verified against the seam's JWKS everywhere. The Host-spoof workaround retired by fixing the tunnel path. Fail-closed stays, but fails LOUD: an identity outage renders as 'identity is down', never as a generic error page." ;
    chorus:implementationPlan "(1) #3878's /clearing move forces the Clearing-door decision — route its auth through the seam in the same change rather than porting the static token. (2) Retire the Cloudflare Host-spoof: tunnel config gains a direct id.* path for server-side grants (Silas, tunnel owner). (3) Loud-fail login page distinguishing identity-down from bad-credentials (the gate-refusal-names-its-state rule applied to the front door)." ;
    chorus:pathToClose "Closed when every public surface's login flows through the seam, the Host-spoof is gone, and an identity outage names itself to the visitor." ;
    chorus:gaps "Single instance, hard-fail dependency for all login (observed: CSS down = login error page). Host-spoof workaround in login.handler.ts is load-bearing. Clearing public door still uses a static bridge token, not seam identity. No Document instance linked yet (hasDesignDoc floor unmet across all Services — Silas review point 3)." ;
    chorus:notInScope "AuthZ of any kind: allow-lists, role grants, per-surface permissions (roles domain / consuming apps). Session STORAGE (gathering's sessions.db). Nostr key derivation for Buzz (#3674 bar: derived creds bound to Principals — a consumer of this seam, not part of it)." .

# Instances observed (from instances-observed.json; the harvester will own
# these rows in the graph — listed here only as the deploys-mapping spec):
#   instance-library-com.gathering.blockverse? NO — outside (app).
#   CSS pod runs as... (launchd label verified below in pair review)
#   deploys→ chorus:service-identity: the CSS pod unit on library.
